The upstream source tree remains unmodified in the development checkout.
scripts/prepare-core.ps1 applies explicit adaptations to generated source:
transport injection; dependency-free diagnostics; safe disabling of external
program execution; strict unsupported-feature handling; RFC 1205 Query,
client reply, immediate/alternate read and Save Screen corrections; transparent
data handling; blink restoration; explicit code-page failure; Reset state.
src/core-adapter contains the replacement controller, logger and transport seam.

No upstream runtime JARs, Log4j, Jython, JT400, mail or PDF dependencies are
included in the application.

Packaged application images include complete application/build/test source and
the pinned upstream source under app/source, also supplied as Fish-source.zip.
Keep that matching source and these notices with redistributed application images.
Do not distribute just the executable or JAR without the corresponding source
and all applicable GPL obligations.

The bundled runtime is generated from Eclipse Temurin OpenJDK 21.0.8+9 by default
(or the JDK explicitly selected for the build). Its module-specific licenses and
notices are in runtime/legal. OpenJDK uses GPL version 2 with the Classpath
Exception; see those notices. Temurin release/source information:
https://github.com/adoptium/temurin21-binaries/releases/tag/jdk-21.0.8%2B9
https://github.com/openjdk/jdk21u/tree/jdk-21.0.8%2B9
Use an appropriately maintained JDK 21 build for deployment and retain its notices.

Protocol references: RFC 1205, RFC 4777, RFC 854/855/856, RFC 885,
RFC 1091 and RFC 1572. These are referenced specifications, not bundled code.
